    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customer-code de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\nThe `customerCode(Owner)` method computes a base code formatted `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. I added a `deduplicateCustomerCode(String base)` helper that:\n\n1. Collects all existing owners' non-null `customerCode` values into a set (via the existing `clinicService.findAllOwners()` pattern used elsewhere in the class).\n2. Returns the base code unchanged when no existing owner holds it.\n3. Otherwise appends `-<n>`, starting at `n = 2` and incrementing until it finds the smallest `n \u2265 2` that produces a code no existing owner holds (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`).\n\nI also updated the Javadoc to document the collision-handling behavior. The new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` and the entire suite pass.",
